        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T22:12:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like is_identified is conceptually redundant with discovery. Getting rid of it without loss of functionality would involve validating identity response VDMs inside TCPMv1 before calling dfp_consume_cable, which it currently doesn\u0027t do. That fits somewhat with this CL, but it could also be part of a whole larger effort to get rid of this struct entirely. I\u0027m inclined to leave it for now but open to persuasion.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 551,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 551,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "9b3bd01cc2331ce99dd7e54434457ee3259d115f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1705566f_306b63b0",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 551,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-01T22:17:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect we have a general cleanup task in our future to remove pd_cable entirely from v2.  The attributes are already redundant with the identity discovery information, and these CLs make the discovery mode fields redundant as well. \n\nUltimately, we\u0027ll probably keep the flags and last message support in here for v1 to use, but the shared code should move away from this structure once discovery is complete.",
      "parentUuid": "63f12748_a8ee2ea2",
